Feature: Add fourth serial lifecycle smoke marker
  As a nmg-sdlc smoke operator
  I want a fourth byte-stable serial lifecycle marker
  So that serial delivery can be proven by a minimal, documented, automatically checked artifact

  @SCN001
  Scenario: Root marker has exact bytes
    Given the enhancement has been implemented
    When root LIVE_SMOKE_D.txt is read as bytes
    Then the file exists
    And its complete byte sequence is "LIVE_SMOKE_D" followed by exactly one LF byte and no other bytes

  @SCN002
  Scenario: README links and describes the marker
    Given the same implemented checkout
    When README.md is read
    Then it links to root LIVE_SMOKE_D.txt
    And it describes that marker as the fourth serial lifecycle smoke marker whose content is exactly "LIVE_SMOKE_D" followed by one newline

  @SCN003
  Scenario: Canonical marker and README mention pass deterministically
    Given LIVE_SMOKE_D.txt has exactly the bytes "LIVE_SMOKE_D\n"
    And README.md links and describes that marker
    When the focused live-smoke-d Jest test runs from scripts
    Then the Jest process exits zero
    And the test verifies both the file bytes and the README mention
    And the test uses no network, clock, or environment-dependent input

  @SCN004
  Scenario Outline: Marker or README drift fails the contract test
    Given the live-smoke-d contract inputs are <drift state>
    When the focused live-smoke-d Jest test runs from scripts
    Then the Jest process exits non-zero

    Examples:
      | drift state                                                         |
      | LIVE_SMOKE_D.txt missing                                            |
      | LIVE_SMOKE_D.txt present with bytes "LIVE_SMOKE_D" and no newline   |
      | LIVE_SMOKE_D.txt present with bytes "LIVE_SMOKE_D\n\n"             |
      | LIVE_SMOKE_D.txt present with bytes "live-smoke-d\n"               |
      | canonical LIVE_SMOKE_D.txt bytes and README omits LIVE_SMOKE_D.txt  |
